{
    "_comment": [
        "Kayra servo map: the single place where a servo channel number gets a meaning.",
        "Channel number == ServoCluster pin number on the Pimoroni servo2040 == index in the",
        "18-float vector used by the 'sss' / 'sas' / 'snp' serial commands and by servoControl.json.",
        "",
        "Convention: even index = right side, odd index = left side, ordered bottom-up per leg.",
        "",
        "Fields per servo:",
        "  index           channel on the servo2040 (0..17)",
        "  name            short id, used by the inverse kinematics and by tools",
        "  label           human readable name shown in the UIs",
        "  side            R, L or C (centre / not mirrored)",
        "  chain           legR, legL, armR, armL, spine, head or none",
        "  part            the printed part this servo drives, cf Pics/parts_naming.png",
        "  mujocoActuator  actuator name in mujoco/kayraLowerBody.xml, null if not simulated yet",
        "  mujocoSign      multiply the servo angle by this before sending it to MuJoCo",
        "  min / max       software limits in degrees, clamped by host and firmware",
        "  observed        [min, max] actually used by the 23 poses in servoControl.json",
        "  enabled         false = channel not wired to anything, always driven to 0",
        "  verified        false = the joint assignment is inferred, not confirmed on hardware",
        "  limitsVerified  false = min/max are provisional, not measured mechanical limits",
        "",
        "To confirm the unverified entries on the real robot, run:",
        "  python3 software/host/tools/identifyServo.py"
    ],
